<title>USA: J.C. Penney may issue $2.0 billion in debt.</title>
<headline>J.C. Penney may issue $2.0 billion in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>J.C. Penney Co. Inc. is expected to tap the corporate bond market soon with a $2.0 billion multi-tranche debt offering, underwriters said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The offering, which is expected to be underwritten by Credit Suisse First Boston, is expected to include five, 10 and 30-year maturities, they said.</p>
<p>Credit Suisse First Boston had no comment on the offering.</p>
</text>
